           Canadian Clinics Improve Care Delivery, Cut Costs
            With CACH�-based Asystar Medical Record Solutions

CAMBRIDGE, Mass.�February 23, 2004�InterSystems Corporation today
spotlighted clinics in two Canadian provinces that have reached the twin
goals of quality care delivery and cost reduction with practice
management software built on the post-relational CACH� database. The
Dorval Family Health Network and the Brandon Clinic are achieving their
medical and business objectives with Asystar Medical Record Solutions,
an InterSystems application partner. The successful implementations were
part of a round of announcements made by InterSystems at the HIMSS 2004
conference in Orlando, Fla.

InterSystems, which develops and markets the CACH� database, is the
leading provider of database technology in healthcare. All of the top 10
hospitals in America, as rated by U.S. News and World Report, are
running CACH�-based systems. Asystar Medical Record Solutions
specializes in providing medical practice management software with
computerized medical records for clients across Canada and the United
States.

RAD Platform Plus Sophisticated Querying Help Recover Revenue

Located in Oakville, Ontario, the Dorval Family Health Network was the
first Family Health Network (FHN) in Onatiro. Under the FHN model,
physicians work with other healthcare professionals to provide primary
care and advice on a 24 x 7 basis. �The emphasis here is on prevention
and comprehensive care,� explains Dr. George Southey, lead physician of
the Dorval Family Health Network. CACH� rapid application development
capabilities played a major role when the physician group transitioned
from fee-for-service to the FHN model, according to Southey.

�The CACH� platform enabled rapid, easy development of new functions. As
a result, Asystar   was able to build additional features, including the
capability to create and maintain a patient roster, the ability to
update demographics from government reports and the ability to make the
changes needed to meet standards that are rewarded with the new payment
system,� Southey says. �For example, Asystar built a customized routine
that made it possible to synchronize our patient registration data with
the registration information of the government of Ontario in just six
hours. That includes creating and fully testing the functionality so it
could be rolled into production.�

Asystar also built a sophisticated querying capability on the CACH�
platform that generates automatic reminders of required preventive
procedures when a patient�s record is displayed. The FHN model includes
specific preventive and immunization targets, including: providing flu
immunizations for 80 percent of the patient population over the age of
65; pap smears for 80 percent of the target population; mammograms for
75 percent of women ages 50-70; and complete childhood immunizations for
95 percent of the target group.

Using CACH�-based Asystar functions such as the automatic reminders,
each of the six physicians within the Dorval Family Health Network will
achieve the stated maximum thresholds by the annual deadline, according
to Southey. �We�ve more than doubled our achievement rate,� he says.
�The services prompted by the reminders mean improved care delivery, and
they are also a direct source of increased revenue under the FHN
system.�

Performance, Reliability is Critical to Practice Success

CACH�-based Asystar has had a similarly positive impact on the bottom
line of the Brandon Clinic, a 33-physician facility with a full lab and
X-ray, in Brandon, Manitoba. �We make extensive use of the Asystar
online laboratory and consultation modules, which quickly eliminated
paper shuffling throughout the organization,� says Andy Brown,
administrator at the clinic. �By cutting paperwork, physicians are able
to see more patients, and that means an increased revenue stream.

�The reliability of the CACH� database and the Asystar application is
very impressive,� Brown continues. �Additionally, CACH� delivers
performance at the speed physicians expect and require.� Overall
satisfaction with the system rose even more when users began accessing
the application via the Web. �Physicians are now able to work securely
from their homes, and installation cost and time have been significantly
decreased,� Brown says. �Overall, CACH� and Asystar have proven to be
extremely cost-effective.�

Expansion in the Canadian market is a part of InterSystems� growth
strategy, according to InterSystems Vice President of Strategic Planning
Paul Grabscheid. �We�re extremely pleased by the increase in market
share that Canada-based application partners like Asystar are beginning
to see,� he says. �We are committed to supporting these firms and their
customers with ongoing R&D initiatives to ensure they can leverage
technology breakthroughs as rapidly as possible.�

About InterSystems

Headquartered in Cambridge, Massachusetts, InterSystems Corporation
(www.InterSystems.com) has served the needs of IT organizations and
independent software vendors for more than two decades. InterSystems'
showcase products, the CACH� post-relational database and the Ensemble
integration platform, enable the rapid creation and fast integration of
high-performance applications. Over four million people use
